{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794243828,"nonce":"5T7QuidtAe450hzIupOFXl3lLJg=","title":"jno.precond.form(complex terms, inner=ams()) hands AMS the real 2n block","message":"_Form is not complex_native, so a complex form solved with precond=form([...], inner=jno.precond.ams()) runs on the fused real-equivalent block, and the auxiliary form is assembled as a real 2n block too. The inner AMS then refuses it with a misleading message: 'this operator is 2n x 2n but the edge (H(curl)) space has n DOFs, so it is a MIXED system'. The system is not mixed.\n\nReproduction: a complex N1E Maxwell form (curl-curl - k^2 eps mass plus a -1j k face term), with precond=jno.precond.form([curlcurl - (1 - 0.5j) k^2 mass, local faces], inner=jno.precond.ams()) and linear=jno.solve.fgmres(...). This is the complex-shifted twin used to precondition indefinite time-harmonic Maxwell.\n\nFix direction: _Form.complex_native follows its inner spec; the complex auxiliary is then assembled as A_r + i A_i on n, reduced per leg like the system operator. The AMS error should say 'real-equivalent block' when the size is exactly 2 x the edge count.","files":null}]}